<title>FRANCE: EU grain export commitments reach 2.466 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>EU grain export commitments reach 2.466 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union grain export commitments up to August 12 rose 68 percent over last year, official figures showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Figures supplied by member country officials showed grain earmarked for export between July 1, 1997 and August 12, 1997 totalled 2.466 million tonnes against 1.467 million during the same period last year.</p>
<p>Exports of commercial soft wheat grain reached 864,000 tonnes against 186,000 a year ago. Soft wheat flour exports jumped to 1.223 million tonnes from 818,000, but barley exports declined to 150,000 tonnes from 205,0000.</p>
<p>Last Thursday, the European Union granted licences to export 85,000 tonnes of soft wheat, 75,500 tonnes of barley and 9,218 tonnes of rye.  </p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5432</p>
